libssc (0.4.4-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Restore 0002-libssc-light-four-element.patch and add
    0003-libssc-light-trim-padding.patch. The previous 0.4.4-3 (upstream
    parsing) shipped a desktop-visible ambient light sensor that always read
    0 lux, which is worse than the patch it replaced.
  * Measured on marble with 0002 present: the sensor works and reports a real
    value, but only in intensity[1]. A 120 s capture in daylight gave
    [0] = 0.0, [1] = 208.94, [2] = gain = 1.0, [3] = integration = 1024.0,
    accuracy 3. Upstream master and Alpine/pmOS (which build vanilla 0.4.4
    with no patches) read intensity[0], so on that stack the value is 0
    forever; device pages listing the ambient light sensor as working
    describe the sensor being enumerated.
  * 0003 additionally trims trailing zero padding before unpacking: the
    first report after enable is a zero-filled placeholder whose 4-byte
    padding protobuf-c rejects as an invalid tag, which is what produced
    "Failed to unpack light measurement message" right after enabling.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:45:00 +0800

libssc (0.4.4-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop 0002-libssc-light-four-element.patch. It only picked a different
    element of the intensity array; the ambient light sensor on marble is
    unusable either way: the firmware report ends in four zero bytes that
    protobuf-c rejects as an invalid tag (fixed by trimming the padding, see
    the worklog), and even then all three reported intensities are 0.0 with
    accuracy 3, unaffected by screen brightness, so the desktop would show a
    permanently dark room. Shipping the patch implied a working ALS that
    does not exist; the package now keeps upstream's parsing behaviour.
  * Accelerometer, gyroscope, compass and proximity are unaffected: the
    light sensor simply reports 0 while everything else keeps working.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0800

libssc (0.4.4-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Light sensor: handle the four-element intensity layout the Xiaomi marble /
    AMS TCS3701 combo sends ([0] = unused 0.0, [1] = Lux, [2] = gain,
    [3] = integration time). ssc-sensor-light.proto documents two elements
    ([0] = Lux, [1] = raw sensor value) which is what most firmwares send, so
    the parser unconditionally reported intensity[0] - on marble that pinned
    the sensor at 0.0 lx forever (iio-sensor-proxy and everything on top of it
    saw 0 lux) while the real value sat in intensity[1]: 211.7 lx in one
    60 s capture, 242.2 lx in the next, both with accuracy 3. Pick [1] when
    four elements are present.
  * Packaging moves to upstream 0.4.4 (the version already running on the
    device; the previous local entry was 0.4.0-2).

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:25:00 +0800

libssc (0.4.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add python3-dev to Build-Depends. Upstream's meson.build descends into
    mocking/ unconditionally, and mocking/ hard-requires a Python installation
    with headers: it installs ssc-server/ssc-server-tests into bindir and the
    generated protobuf Python bindings ship in the package, so this is not
    test-only scaffolding. Skipping dh_auto_test is not enough; the build
    itself needs Python.h.

