libssc (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of libssc 0.4.0
    (codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/libssc), the Qualcomm Sensor Core library
    that iio-sensor-proxy builds against with -Dssc-support=enabled. Debian
    and Ubuntu do not ship libssc at all, so their iio-sensor-proxy silently
    builds without SSC support.
  * One binary package, as in sheng_fedora_packages/libssc: upstream installs
    libssc.so.2, ssccli, the public headers and libssc.pc unconditionally, and
    the headers/pc are what the iio-sensor-proxy build needs.
  * debian/patches/wait-for-qmi-service.patch: retry the QRTR node lookup for
    the SSC service for a few seconds. The DSP side publishes that service a
    few seconds into the boot, and this rootfs has no initramfs to order
    against, so the single-shot lookup loses the race and iio-sensor-proxy
    then exits with "No sensors or missing kernel drivers" until something
    restarts it.
  * Tests are skipped: upstream's suite runs the library against a Python
    mock QRTR server, which is not part of the shipped library.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:27:00 +0800
